  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Youth Leaders for Project Y</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Youth leader exchange program is attached to Project Y. The project is about strengthening the capacity of youth to take leadership to end teenage pregnancies in selected districts in Uganda. It will target youth-led (leader is below 30 years) grass roots organizations and empower them to manage their organizations progressively and sustainably.  The overall aim of the youth leaders is to center young people in development solutions. They will lead research, develop materials, train volunteers in organizational development, advocacy, volunteerism, SRHR and gender equality, support SRHR youth friendly service provision and Income Generating Activities (IGA) establishment. The youth leaders will also monitor and evaluate project performance. The partnership benefits by having skilled and competent people to implement international projects.</narrative>
  </description>
